  "@@x-review-note": "⚠ MANDATORY pre-release native-speaker review.  isiZulu is a Bantu language with noun-class agreement that English-trained translators routinely get subtly wrong; cannabis-specific terminology in particular (curing, strain, IPM, VPD) lacks canonical isiZulu equivalents and tends to be code-switched to English in real grower conversation.  The translation below favours readability over literary purity — short, declarative phrasing common in modern South African mobile-app vernacular — but it is NOT a substitute for review by a fluent isiZulu UX writer.  Specific terms to flag:  • 'insangu' is the historical isiZulu word for cannabis (Apple/Google listings prefer this over loanwords); kept where the word 'cannabis' would appear in the English source.  • 'ukuvuthwa' is used for 'curing' (verb sense 'to ripen / mature') — closest semantic match; growers may prefer the English 'curing' code-switched.  • 'I-VPD' / 'i-IPM' kept as English loanwords with noun-class i- prefix — standard modern Zulu pattern for technical acronyms.",

